# v1.5.7 089y — npm tarball hygiene.
#
# `package.json`'s `files` allowlist controls what `npm pack`
# includes. Without a .npmignore, `__pycache__` directories under
# `quality_playbook_cli/_bundle/bin/` (created when Python imports
# the staged modules during the worker's pre-flight test runs)
# get swept into the tarball — shipping platform/version-specific
# `.pyc` artifacts. This file excludes that compiled cruft so
# `npm pack` ships only the source files the wheel + clone install.
#
# Mirrors the `bin/build_channel_package.stage()` exclusion list
# (089y T-B): both channels must agree on what's excluded so the
# 4-surface bundle-parity contract holds — the .py set the wheel
# ships, the .py set the npm tarball ships, and `_bundle_files()`
# all stay aligned.

# Python compiled artifacts (the load-bearing 089y exclusion)
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo

# macOS Finder metadata (incidental cruft)
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store

# Editor / OS junk that may land in the data dir during dev
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# Build output dirs (regenerated each publish; never source)
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/

# The worker's local-only artifacts that shouldn't end up in any
# adopter tarball even if they leak into the data tree
quality/logs/
quality/previous_runs/
quality.previous-bootstrap-*/
quality.sonnet-killed-*/
